Problem Name:
Sliding Window with Two Pointers

Time Complexity:
O(n+n)

Space Complexity:
O(1)

Approach:
1. Maintain a sliding window using two pointers l and r.
2. Expand the window by moving r and count the number of zeroes.
3. If zeroes become greater than k, shrink the window from the left.
4. While shrinking, decrease zero count whenever a zero leaves the window.
5. Update the maximum length of the valid window at each step.



class Solution {
    public int longestOnes(int[] arr, int k) {
        int l=0;
        int r=0;
        int zeroes=0;
        int maxLen=0;
        while(r<arr.length){
            if(arr[r]==0) zeroes++;
            while(zeroes>k){
                if(arr[l]==0) zeroes--;
                l++;
            }
            maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, r-l+1);
            r++;
        }
        return maxLen;
    }
}
